# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages / Netlify.
#
# TanStack Router does client-side routing, so every unknown URL must
# fall through to index.html and let React take over. Without this rule,
# /download, /profile, /bookings/xyz etc. all 404 on refresh or direct-
# link.
#
# The `!` on the second column of the first line would exempt some paths
# if we needed to; we don't — every path is a React route.
#
# SVC-343: /.well-known/* is served verbatim (passthrough), NOT rewritten
# to index.html. Google's App Links verifier does an exact-fetch of
# /.well-known/assetlinks.json and expects JSON — if the SPA catch-all
# below rewrote it to HTML the verification would silently fail. Static
# files take precedence over _redirects in Cloudflare Pages, so this
# explicit rule is belt-and-suspenders, but documenting the intent at
# the point of risk is cheap and matters more than one line of config.
# Must come BEFORE the catch-all; Cloudflare evaluates rules top-down.
/.well-known/*  /.well-known/:splat  200
/*    /index.html   200
